Is it
possible to use obsCovs to estimate lambda, gamma, or omega? For example, I
have been playing with the alfl0506 data and pcountOpen script from the January
Webinar. When I try to include time as a covariate to help estimate lambda like
this:

(fm5 <-
pcountOpen(~time, ~1, ~1, ~1, alfl.umf, K=30))

I get this
error:

in
model.frame.default(lamformula, siteCovs, na.action = NULL) :

  object is not a matrix

The reason I
ask is that I am hoping to use monthly fruiting of tree species in three different sites as covariates
to explain monthly bird counts. I don't think I can include fruiting as
siteCovs because fruiting is not a constant feature of my sites – it changes
each month.

I have attached
an example spreadsheet showing how I think I would need to setup my data to use
pcountOpen.  Though I've only included 6
dates, I have 18 dates in my full data set. I welcome any suggestions.

Thanks,
Rhine

