Hi Manuel,

You can ignore the "primaryPeriod" argument if the time between primary periods is constant, which is true in your case. The only thing you need to do is add 3 columns of NAs so that there are 4 columns for each year (you only have one column for 2008). If your matrix is called y, something like this should work:

y2 <- cbind(y, matrix(NA, nrow(y), 3))
umf <- unmarkedFramePCO(y = y2, numPrimary=4)

Richard
